/-!
# Set (d), master `I₁₂`: the integrals `∫₀¹ f_a(t) logⁱ t logʲ (1 + t) dt` in closed form

The 25 integrals `i12HSK a i j = ∫₀¹ f_a(t) logⁱ t logʲ (1 + t) dt` with `i + j ≤ 4`
(`a = 0` with `j ≥ 1`, and `a = -1`), which carry the Taylor coefficients of `P(cε - 1, ε)`
through order `4`. By `QED.ThreeLoopD.i12HSK_eq` each is `i! j!` times a sum of alternating
harmonic polylogarithms at `1` over the shuffles of `0ⁱ` and `(-1)ʲ`; the shuffles are expanded
by `simp` and the values are those of the library (`QED.Polylog.HPLValues`,
`QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt4`, `QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt5A`–`QED.Polylog.HPLValuesAlt5D`,
`QED.Polylog.HPLValuesTrailing` and the relation files), in the basis `log 2`, `π`, `ζ(3)`,
`ζ(5)`, `Li₄(1/2)`, `Li₅(1/2)`.

The statements were generated by a script (the HPL values were read off the library files and
the shuffles expanded symbolically); the proofs are checked by Lean.

## Main results

* `QED.ThreeLoopD.i12HSK_zero_0_1` … `QED.ThreeLoopD.i12HSK_negOne_4_0`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Real QED.Polylog QED.Polylog.HPL QED.Polylog.HPL.Letter

namespace QED.ThreeLoopD

theorem i12HSK_zero_0_1 :
    i12HSK Letter.zero 0 1 =
      1 / 12 * π ^ 2 := by
  rw [(i12HSK_eq (by decide)).2]
  simp only [List.replicate, shuffle_nil_left, List.map_cons, List.map_nil, List.sum_cons,
    List.sum_nil]
  rw [hpl_zero_negOne_at_one]
  norm_num
  ring

